<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matadi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matadi is the chief seaport of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-the-congo">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a> and capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> Central province, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-river">Congo River</a> about 150 kilometres from the Atlantic, below the rapids that block navigation upstream. Founded in 1879 in the time of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-morton-stanley">Henry Morton Stanley</a>, it became the terminus of the railway to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinshasa">Léopoldville</a>, now Kinshasa, completed in 1898.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matadi.jpg" alt="Matadi" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MONUSCO/Myriam Asmani · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Matadi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
